<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mòine Mhòr</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Moine Mhor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mòine Mhòr, Gaelic for 'great moss', is a raised bog in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilmartin">Kilmartin Glen</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a>, one of the largest remaining in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and a national nature reserve. The rocky hill of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunadd">Dunadd</a>, the chief fortress of the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, rises from the bog beside the River Add.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moine-mhor.jpg" alt="Mòine Mhòr" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Patrick Mackie · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moine_Mhor_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1372739.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
